---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy — Formation.Legal"
  description="The rigorous research methodology and editorial independence standards behind Formation.Legal."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="mb-10 border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] sm:text-4xl">Editorial Policy & Methodology</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Last updated: April 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg">
      <p>
        Formation.Legal is engineered to be the definitive decision engine for non-US founders entering the US ecosystem. To achieve this, we adhere to a strict editorial policy.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Independence First</h2>
      <p>
        Our research and editorial team operates entirely independently from our revenue and partnership teams.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No Pay-to-Play:</strong> Providers cannot pay for higher ratings, better placements in the Route Planner, or removal of negative facts.</li>
        <li><strong>Data-Driven Reality:</strong> We prioritize operational reality over marketing claims. If a provider claims easy bank access but the route varies materially for non-residents, we publish that operational risk.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. The Route-Based Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        We do not believe in "Best Overall LLC Services". A service that is perfect for a US resident might be a poor fit for a non-US resident who needs an EIN path and a compatible banking or payout route.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our methodology evaluates providers, states, and entity types based on <strong>specific routes</strong> (e.g., Country + Business Model + Payment Goal).
      </p>

      <h2>3. Trust Layer & Source Logs</h2>
      <p>
        We believe in showing our work. Where possible, we publish the underlying source logs, state statutes, and test results that inform our guides in the <code>/research</code> section. Every guide includes metadata detailing its originality, AI-assistance level, and the specific author or researcher responsible for the content.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Updates and Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        US corporate compliance (like the CTA/BOI reporting rules) and banking regulations change rapidly. We actively monitor these changes. When a material change occurs that affects our recommendations, we update our guides and Route Planner logic, logging the changes clearly.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you spot an inaccuracy in our research, we want to know. Please contact our editorial team.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
